codemap 8
path feature-add-step
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note Add code to the path being read, from wherever it is shown. The reader reaches for it to turn code already on screen into a step without switching to the CLI (the human builds paths by hand). In the Source view, select lines (click, shift-click) and press the toolbar's add button, which names them ('add lines 12-20 as a step'). On a Symbols row or a References caller or callee row, press '+ step', shown while the row is hovered, to add that symbol whole; 'add step' under the References heading adds the selected symbol. On an off-path graph node, '+ step' adds its symbol. The step is authored by the human and hangs under the target (see feature-choose-target), except a graph node revealed as a callee of a step, which hangs under that step. The same lines under the same parent again is refused with the step's number; adding moves neither the selection nor the target, so the next add lands beside this one. The status names the new step's number and parent.

